@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
title TARGET DESIGN ONLY: PowerShell installation and rollback
class "install.ps1" as installer {
 selected clients : Claude | Codex | Grok | Cline
 SupportsShouldProcess / WhatIf
 Invoke installation or explicit rollback
}
class "Install-Discovery.psm1" as discovery {
 Resolve-AgentExecutable(client)
 Get-AgentCapabilities(executable, version)
 New-InstallPlan(selectedClients)
}
class "Install-Configuration.psm1" as merge {
 Read-ClientConfiguration()
 Compare-ManagedEntries(plan)
 Set-ManagedEntries(plan)
 preserve unrelated keys and instruction sections
}
class "Install-Rollback.psm1" as rollback {
 Copy-VerifiedOriginal(path)
 Save-ChangeJournal(preimage, managedPatch, hashes)
 Restore-ManagedChanges(journal, currentConfig)
 retain originals and report conflicts
}
class "InstallPlan" as plan <<data>> {
 selectedClients, executablePaths, versions, capabilities
 configPaths, managedEntries, instructionSectionIds
 v1ToV2BehaviorNotice, requiredApprovals
}
class "ChangeJournal" as journal <<data>> {
 transactionId, path, originalCopyPath, originalHash
 priorManagedValue, appliedManagedValue, appliedHash
 rollbackStatus, conflictPaths
}
class "User configuration" as config <<external data>> {
 selected client MCP registrations
 trusted caller/workspace binding
 no auto-approve write/resume-write/escalation
}
installer --> discovery
discovery --> plan
installer --> merge
merge --> rollback : backup before mutation
rollback --> journal
merge --> config : patch owned entries
rollback --> config : conditional surgical restore
note bottom of rollback
WhatIf performs no writes or agent execution.
On later unrelated edits: retain those edits.
On same managed-field conflict: report and do not overwrite.
Windows/Linux target; existing macOS installer stays out of scope.
end note
@enduml
